@startuml
title KiwiDB — State Machine: SSTable file lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Writing : SSTableWriter created (state OPEN)

state Writing {
  [*] --> Buffering
  Buffering --> Buffering : put(key, seq, ts, value)\n(ascending keys)
  Buffering --> Buffering : block full -> flush block,\nadd to sparse index + bloom
}

Writing --> Complete : finish() / finish_sync()\nwrites index.bin, filter.bin,\nthen meta.json LAST
note right of Complete
  meta.json present =
  "table is complete".
  A crash before this leaves an
  incomplete folder, ignored on recovery.
end note

Complete --> Live : registered in SSTableManager\n(reader open, refcount = 0)

state Live {
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Reading : open_reader() (refcount++)
  Reading --> Idle : reader released (refcount--)
}

Live --> MarkedForDeletion : superseded by compaction\n(mark_for_deletion)

state MarkedForDeletion {
  [*] --> Draining
  Draining --> Draining : in-flight reads finishing
}

MarkedForDeletion --> Deleted : refcount == 0\n-> files removed, cache invalidated
Deleted --> [*]

@enduml
